+##
+## Template Type:
+## -------------
+## This is a velocity template, see: http://velocity.apache.org/
+##
+## Template File Names and extensions:
+## ----------------------------------
+## Gerrit will use templates ending in ".vm" but will ignore templates ending
+## in ".vm.example".  If a .vm template does not exist, the default internal
+## gerrit template which is the same as the .vm.example will be used.  If you
+## want to override the default template, copy the .vm.exmaple file to a .vm
+## file and edit it appropriately.
+##
+## Template Purposes;
+## -----------------
+## The NewChange.vm template will determine the contents of the email related
+## to a user submitting a new change for review (see also ChangeSubject.vm and
+## ChangeFooter.vm).
+##
+## Template Resources:
+## ------------------
+## Writting templates for gerrit emails is likely to require some basic
+## knowledge of the class structure to be useful, so browsing the source
+## code might be necessary.  All outgoing emails have the following
+## variables available to them:
+##
+##  $email          a reference to the class constructing the current email.
+##                  With this reference it is possible to call any public
+##                  method on the email class.
+##
+##  $messageClass   a String containing the messageClass
+##
+##  StringUtils     a reference to the apaache StringUtils class.  This can
+##                  be very usefull for formatting strings.
+##
+##
+## All change related emails have the following additional variables available
+## to them:
+##
+##  $change         a reference to the current change object
+##
+##  $branch         a reference to the bracn of this change
+##
+##  $projectName    the name of this change's project
+##
+##  $patchSet       a reference to the current patchSet
+##
+##  $patchSetInfo   a reference to the current patchSetInfo
+##
+## Of particular interest to this class is likely:
+##
+##  $email.reviewersNames  a list of the names of each reviewer.
+##
+#set ($destination = "Change $change.key.abbreviate() for $change.dest.shortName in $projectName:")
+#if($email.reviewersNames)
+Hello $StringUtils.join($email.reviewersNames, ' ,'),
+
+I'd like you to do a code review.#if($email.changeUrl)  Please visit
+
+    $email.changeUrl
+
+to review the following change:
+#end
+
+$destination
+#else
+$destination
+#if($email.changeUrl)
+
+    $email.changeUrl
+
+#end
+#end
+
+$email.changeDetail
+  git pull ssh://$email.sshHost/$projectName $patchSet.refName
